<title>USA: SunAmerica says variable annuity sales up.</title>
<headline>SunAmerica says variable annuity sales up.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>SunAmerica Inc said its variable annuity product sales doubled during fiscal 1996, reaching $1.7 billion, compared with $858 million last year.</p>
<p>Fourth quarter variable annuity product sales totaled $472 million, up 66 percent over last year's comparable figure of $284 million.</p>
<p>SunAmerica Monday announced preliminary unaudited earnings of $274.4 million or $1.95 per share for its fiscal year ended September 30, 1996, up 37 percent on a per-share basis from $194.2 million or $1.42 per share in 1995.</p>
</text>
